        {
          "id": 666818931,
          "type": null,
          "body": "The old code assumes that input buffer is always less than output buffer:\n\n```\n#0  gz_head (state=0x612000000340) at ../wiretap/file_wrappers.c:881\n#1  0x00007ffff7de7ccb in fill_out_buffer (state=0x612000000340)\n    at ../wiretap/file_wrappers.c:895\n#2  0x00007ffff7de7acb in file_read (buf=0x7fffffffb5a0, len=4, \n    file=0x612000000340) at ../wiretap/file_wrappers.c:1577\n#3  0x00007ffff7dfe7fb in wtap_read_bytes (fh=0x612000000340, buf=0x7fffffffb5a0, \n    count=4, err=0x7fffffffc320, err_info=0x7fffffffc330)\n    at ../wiretap/wtap.c:1629\n#4  0x00007ffff7dcf5f2 in libpcap_open (wth=0x60f000000130, err=0x7fffffffc320, \n    err_info=0x7fffffffc330) at ../wiretap/libpcap.c:130\n#5  0x00007ffff7dd9a8c in wtap_open_offline (\n    filename=0x7fffffffd569 \"suite_text2pcap.case_text2pcap_pcap.test_text2pcap_wpa_induction_pcap.testout.pcap\", type=0, err=0x7fffffffc320, \n    err_info=0x7fffffffc330, do_random=0) at ../wiretap/file_access.c:970\n#6  0x000055555565a838 in process_cap_file (\n    filename=0x7fffffffd569 \"suite_text2pcap.case_text2pcap_pcap.test_text2pcap_wpa_induction_pcap.testout.pcap\", need_separator=0) at ../capinfos.c:1194\n#7  0x000055555565990b in main (argc=3, argv=0x7fffffffd0e8) at ../capinfos.c:1851\n(gdb) p state->out.size\n$1 = 131072\n(gdb) p state->in.size\n$2 = 131075\n(gdb) \n```",
