    {
      "id": "507c6b010e8d358ed76ff2f2437bd492e36b67a7",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 668044670,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "> I think all buffer offsets etc should be in `gsize`/`gssize` (size of pointer)\n\nNote that, on Windows, `ws_read()`, which is just `_read()` on Windows with MSVC, takes an `unsigned int` as its third argument and returns an `int`, so you can't read more than 2^31-1 bytes (you could pass up to 2^32-1 as an argument, but, if all the bytes are read, the return value will be negative).\n\nSo we'd have to do more work to support buffers bigger than 2^30 bytes in size.\n\n> and file offsets in `gint64` (for largefile support on 32bit).\n\nThey already are.  See #17301.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-09-02T22:30:41.767Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-09-02T22:53:55.060Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 115003140,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 4081,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 668055563,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Interesting, I know almost nothing about Win32 API. I didn't have larger buffers in mind, rather that `gsize/gsszie` are always defined such that pointer arithmetic can be done without casting (still need to consider overflow).",
          "author": {
            "id": 4196846,
            "username": "rigtorp",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Erik Rigtorp",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/e82c2024eea7f3e0cb4a20d77990c263029b0cd2786dff5aea3adcc7b281c87e?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/rigtorp"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-09-02T22:53:55.009Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-09-02T22:53:55.009Z",
